<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agios Nikolaos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agios Nikolaos is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mirabello">Gulf of Mirabello</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, and the capital of the regional unit of Lasithi. It stands on the site of Lato pros Kamara, the harbour of the ancient city of Lato, and takes its name from a Byzantine church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-nicholas">Saint Nicholas</a>. The modern town grew in the 19th century and is now a centre of tourism.</p></div>
